IMPORT prelude

§ `CODEX INSURANCE LIMITED — Daily Hospital Income Benefit policy`

-- This file encodes the rules of the policy contract (inputs/chubb-policy.txt)
-- as pure functions of a `Claim` -- it defines no claim data of its own.
--
-- Every time/date fact other than the claimant's age is carried as a NUMBER
-- of months elapsed since the policy's effective date, per the task's
-- instruction that all query facts (bar age) are given relative to the
-- effective date, so no calendar-date arithmetic is needed anywhere here.
--
-- Per the task's instructions, §1.1(1) "this agreement is signed" and
-- §1.1(2) "the premium ... has been paid" are assumed always to hold, and so
-- are not modelled as facts of a Claim or tested by any rule below.

§§ `§5 Benefit and premium amounts`

`daily hospital income benefit amount in USD` MEANS 500
`premium amount in USD`                       MEANS 2000

§§ `Key thresholds used throughout (§1.3, §2.2, §3.1(5), §4.6)`

-- §1.3: written confirmation of the wellness visit is due no later than the
-- 7th month anniversary of the effective date.
`wellness confirmation deadline in months` MEANS 7

-- §4.6: the policy term is one year from the effective date.
`policy term in months` MEANS 12

-- §2.2: the benefit is payable for at most 365 days of continuous confinement.
`maximum benefit days` MEANS 365

-- §3.1(5): the age exclusion threshold.
`age exclusion threshold` MEANS 80

§ `The shape of a claim`

-- One `Claim` bundles every fact that §1-§3 of the policy need, in order to
-- decide whether a given hospitalization is covered. Every duration is
-- months since the effective date (see the file header); `age at
-- hospitalization` is the one absolute figure the task tells us to keep
-- absolute.
DECLARE Claim HAS
    `age at hospitalization`                                          IS A NUMBER
    `months since the effective date at hospitalization`              IS A NUMBER
    `wellness visit occurred within six months of the effective date` IS A BOOLEAN
    `wellness confirmation submission month`                          IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `fraud or misrepresentation`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `confined in a hospital in the United States`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of continuous confinement`                                  IS A NUMBER
    `claim made to the Company`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury arose from skydiving`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury arose from military service`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury arose from firefighter service`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `injury arose from police service`                                IS A BOOLEAN

§ `§1 Policy in effect and conditions`

-- §1.3, evaluated as of the hospitalization: if the confirmation has already
-- been submitted, it must have been submitted by month 7. If it has not yet
-- been submitted, the condition is still "pending" as long as the 7-month
-- deadline has not yet arrived at the time of the hospitalization.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization not yet past the wellness confirmation deadline` claim MEANS
    claim's `months since the effective date at hospitalization` AT MOST `wellness confirmation deadline in months`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness confirmation timely or still pending` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness confirmation submission month`
    WHEN JUST month THEN month AT MOST `wellness confirmation deadline in months`
    WHEN NOTHING     THEN `hospitalization not yet past the wellness confirmation deadline` claim

-- §1.1(3): "The condition set out in Section 1.3 is still pending or has
-- been satisfied in a timely fashion" -- §1.3 itself has two limbs: the
-- visit occurring by month 6, and confirmation of it being supplied by
-- month 7.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 1.3 condition pending or satisfied` claim MEANS
        claim's `wellness visit occurred within six months of the effective date`
    AND `wellness confirmation timely or still pending` claim

-- §4.6 / §1.2 last sentence: the policy automatically ends one year after
-- the effective date.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`hospitalization after the policy term ends` claim MEANS
    claim's `months since the effective date at hospitalization` GREATER THAN `policy term in months`

-- §1.2: cancellation triggers -- fraud/misrepresentation/material
-- withholding, §1.3 not satisfied in a timely fashion, or the policy term
-- having run out.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy canceled` claim MEANS
        claim's `fraud or misrepresentation`
    OR  NOT (`section 1.3 condition pending or satisfied` claim)
    OR  `hospitalization after the policy term ends` claim

-- §1.1: the policy is in effect at the time of the hospitalization.
-- (§1.1(1)-(2), signature and timely payment of premium, are assumed -- see
-- the file header.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`policy in effect` claim MEANS
        `section 1.3 condition pending or satisfied` claim
    AND NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

§ `§2 Benefits`

-- §2.1-§2.3: confinement in a US hospital, within the 365-day cap, with a
-- claim properly made to the Company. (§2.1's own requirement -- that the
-- confinement be "as a result of sickness or accidental Injury" -- is the
-- shared premise of every one of the nine benchmark questions, so it is not
-- separately modelled as a Claim field here.)
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`benefit conditions satisfied` claim MEANS
        claim's `confined in a hospital in the United States`
    AND claim's `days of continuous confinement` AT MOST `maximum benefit days`
    AND claim's `claim made to the Company`

§ `§3 General exclusions`

-- §3.1: sickness or injury "arising directly or indirectly out of" one of
-- four listed activities, or the claimant's age at the time of the
-- hospitalization.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`exclusion applies` claim MEANS
        claim's `injury arose from skydiving`
    OR  claim's `injury arose from military service`
    OR  claim's `injury arose from firefighter service`
    OR  claim's `injury arose from police service`
    OR  claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST `age exclusion threshold`

§ `Top-level decision`

-- Does the policy apply to (i.e. is the benefit payable for) this claim?
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`covered` claim MEANS
        `policy in effect` claim
    AND `benefit conditions satisfied` claim
    AND NOT (`exclusion applies` claim)
